      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary angiography and left ventriculography was performed in 45 coronary patients with stable angina using triombrast and in 45 similar patients using omnipaque. Omnipaque was better tolerated than triombrast. The negative electrocardiographic and hemodynamic side effects were less marked with omnipaque than triombrast. The incidence of complication was lower in patients with omnipaque."},
